[by:Flame-_s]
[00:19.50]This land today, shall draw its last breath
[00:28.22]And take into its ancient depths
[00:36.50]This frail reminder of its giant, dreaming self.
[00:43.15]While I, with human-hindered eyes
[00:49.68]Unequal to the sweeping curve of life,
[00:56.37]Stand on this single print of time.

[01:02.75]Human wheels spin round and round
[01:09.74]While the clock keeps the pace.
[01:15.33]Human wheels spin round and round
[01:23.10]Help the light to my face.

[01:42.58]That time, today, no triumph gains
[01:50.90]At this short success of age.
[01:58.64]This pale reflection of its brave and
[02:03.67]Blundering deed.
[02:06.37]For I, descend from this vault,
[02:12.82]Now dreams beyond my earthly fault
[02:19.46]Knowledge, sure, from the seed.

[02:26.60]Human wheels spin round and round
[02:32.37]While the clock keeps the pace.
[02:38.61]Human wheels spin round and round
[02:46.20]Help the light to my face.

[03:21.29]This land, today, my tears will taste
[03:30.41]And take into its dark embrace.
[03:38.79]This love, who in my beating heart endures,
[03:45.42]Assured, by every sun that burns,
[03:51.22]The dust to which this flesh shall return.
[03:58.74]It is the ancient, dreaming dust of God.

[04:05.52]Human wheels spin round and round
[04:12.25]While the clock keeps the pace.
[04:18.91]Human wheels spin round and round
[04:25.58]Help the light to my face.
[04:32.20]Human wheels spin round and round
[04:38.91]While the clock keeps the pace.
[04:44.92]Human wheels spin round and round
[04:52.30]Help the light to my face.